            <ArticleTitle>A case study on a home-based caregiver-delivered music-with-movement intervention for people with early dementia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2050313X17730264</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/2050313X17730264</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Music has been found to improve sleep and reduce anxiety.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="PURPOSE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">This article reports a 78-year-old Chinese female who had been diagnosed with early dementia underwent an 8-week music-with-movement intervention delivered by her husband at home after being trained in a day care center.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Both the patient and the husband's data were collected through repeated interviews and regular observations.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The results indicated signs of improvement of the patient in terms of sleep quality and depressive symptoms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
